  "reply": "This looks like the UCI Ozone Level Detection data set. It has two versions: \"eighthr\" and \"onehr\", each with 2,536 and 2,534 instances. The 72 features and the \"normal day / ozone day\" classes match. The eighthr version has 2,534 rows and 73 attributes, including a date and the class label, which leaves 72 features once the date is dropped. The OpenML version \"ozone-level-8hr\" has 2,534 rows and 73 columns (72 features plus the class), which fits the description.\n\n{\"name\": \"Ozone Level Detection (ozone-level-8hr)\", \"source\": \"UCI Machine Learning Repository (Zhang et al., 2006); also OpenML ozone-level-8hr\", \"confidence\": 0.85}"
