  "reply": "This feature list matches the UCI Ozone Level Detection data set (Zhang et al.). Its features are hourly wind speed (WSR0-23), temperature (T0-23), and upper-air measurements at 850, 700 and 500 hPa, plus KI, TT, SLP and precipitation. The target is whether a day is an ozone day, and the data covers the Houston, Galveston and Brazoria area. There are two versions, eighthr and onehr.\n\n```json\n{\"name\": \"Ozone Level Detection (eighthr/onehr)\", \"source\": \"UCI Machine Learning Repository; Zhang & Fan, 'Forecasting skewed biased stochastic ozone days'\", \"confidence\": 0.95}\n```"
 },
